Subject: [PATCH] TestSocket: use an unbuffered binary stream

Upstream-Status: Downstream (binary socket command buffering)
Upstream-Reference: https://github.com/ionelmc/python-process-tests

Line buffering does not flush writes to a binary socket makefile.
TestSocket clients then wait for commands to reach the debugger.
Use an unbuffered stream so writes are sent immediately.

diff --git a/src/process_tests.py b/src/process_tests.py
--- a/src/process_tests.py
+++ b/src/process_tests.py
@@ -211,7 +211,7 @@ class TestSocket(PipeBuffer if fcntl else ThreadedBuffer):

     def __init__(self, sock):
         self.sock = sock
-        self.fh = sock.makefile('rbw', buffering=1)
+        self.fh = sock.makefile('rbw', buffering=0)

         if fcntl:
             sock.setblocking(0)
--
